[Applause]  its toppling caused reverberations  worldwide  by the end of sunday the 7th of june  2020 the statue of slave trader edward  colston that had stood for more than 125  years  was at the bottom of bristol harbor  today four of those protesters were  found not guilty of criminal damage  i'm just so overwhelmed because it never  felt like we got we'd get here and now  we're here and this is we just want to  say thank you to so many people because  we have never been alone in this journey  we didn't change history we rectified  his dream  the pulling down of colston statue came  during a black lives matter protest in  the city less than two weeks after the  murder of george floyd in minneapolis  tensions in the city were high  the jury was shown cctv footage of the  defendants and others involved in the  pulling down and rolling of the statue  but in the end the jury sided with the  defense that bristol is better off  without the statue on this plinth that  was described during the trial as a  festering cancer in the city  the statue which has been on display in  a museum since last summer sparked a  nationwide debate over other  controversial monuments  some historians say its removal is  simply part of its history to see it  brought down  uh within the context of a  global protest about persistent forms of  racial inequality that find their roots  in  the history of slavery i think was an  extraordinary moment  for the supporters of the four on trial  this was the right result i think this  is just such a waste of money bringing  this prosecution uh to trial because uh  the people of bristol never wanted the  statue it feels like a very historic  moment bristol has had control of its  own narrative for too long i just took  the control out of bristol's hands  at the end of the two-week trial three  of the defendants left court wearing  t-shirts made by street artist banksy  he said the money raised was so they  could go for a pint for the so-called  colston four it is an historic night of  celebration dan whitehead sky news in  bristol

